        </ul>

        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            For an outdoor flagstone patio, use a breathable penetrating sealer — natural finish if you want the stone to look unchanged, an enhancing one if you want the wet, saturated look. Both let the assembly dry, which is what keeps them from going cloudy.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Save film-forming sealers for stone set in mortar over a solid slab with good drainage, where moisture is not rising from beneath. On a dry-laid patio they are a nearly guaranteed disappointment, and stripping one off flagstone is a job you only want to do once.
          </p>
        </div>

